{"words": [{"text": "أَمْ", "translation": "Or"}, {"text": "تُرِيدُونَ", "translation": "(do) you wish"}, {"text": "أَن", "translation": "that"}, {"text": "تَسْـَٔلُوا۟", "translation": "you ask"}, {"text": "رَسُولَكُمْ", "translation": "your Messenger"}, {"text": "كَمَا", "translation": "as"}, {"text": "سُئِلَ", "translation": "was asked"}, {"text": "مُوسَىٰ", "translation": "Musa"}, {"text": "مِن", "translation": "from"}, {"text": "قَبْلُ ۗ", "translation": "before"}, {"text": "وَمَن", "translation": "And whoever"}, {"text": "يَتَبَدَّلِ", "translation": "exchanges"}, {"text": "ٱلْكُفْرَ", "translation": "[the] disbelief"}, {"text": "بِٱلْإِيمَـٰنِ", "translation": "with [the] faith"}, {"text": "فَقَدْ", "translation": "so certainly"}, {"text": "ضَلَّ", "translation": "he went astray (from)"}, {"text": "سَوَآءَ", "translation": "(the) evenness"}, {"text": "ٱلسَّبِيلِ", "translation": "(of) the way"}], "sahih": "Or do you intend to ask1 your Messenger as Moses was asked before? And whoever exchanges faith for disbelief has certainly strayed from the soundness of the way."}